WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.772 --> 00:00:02.473
"Are you ready?"

2
00:00:02.553 --> 00:00:04.134
Henry asked Maggie.

3
00:00:04.254 --> 00:00:05.415
It was later that day.

4
00:00:05.495 --> 00:00:10.299
The Lemonade Detectives were hiding behind a car parked near Nora's house.

5
00:00:10.319 --> 00:00:16.184
They were getting ready to put the first step of Henry's plan into action.

6
00:00:31.088 --> 00:00:32.049
Maggie made a face.

7
00:00:32.069 --> 00:00:36.051
"Why do I have to be the one to distract Nora?"

8
00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:37.231
she complained.

9
00:00:37.251 --> 00:00:42.054
"You're the only one who can distract her well enough," Henry said.

10
00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:45.316
"Yeah." Cole laughed.

11
00:00:46.477 --> 00:00:50.899
"Nora would never believe it if Henry and I suddenly wanted to play princesses with her!"

12
00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:54.421
"I guess you're right," Maggie said.

13
00:00:54.441 --> 00:00:57.863
"But being a detective is harder than I thought!"

14
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.964
"Good luck."

15
00:01:01.196 --> 00:01:03.238
Henry peeked out from behind the car.

16
00:01:07.342 --> 00:01:08.342
just came outside.

17
00:01:09.644 --> 00:01:11.946
See if you can keep her in the front yard, okay?"

18
00:01:11.966 --> 00:01:16.369
"Okay." Maggie stood up and waved at Nora.

19
00:01:16.389 --> 00:01:18.011
"Hi, Nora!

20
00:01:18.972 --> 00:01:19.732
What are you doing?"

21
00:01:20.193 --> 00:01:21.914
she called in a super-friendly voice.

22
00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.597
"Wow," Cole whispered.

23
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:26.839
"She's a pretty good actress."

24
00:01:27.239 --> 00:01:27.980
Henry grinned.

25
00:01:29.052 --> 00:01:31.574
"Mom always says Maggie is very dramatic.

26
00:01:31.594 --> 00:01:34.057
I guess she's right."

27
00:01:35.077 --> 00:01:37.159
He looked out from behind the car again.

28
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.183
Nora was twirling on her tiptoes while Maggie watched.

29
00:01:41.203 --> 00:01:45.286
"It looks like Nora is distracted," he told Cole.

30
00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:49.270
"We should be able to sneak through the neighbors' yard so she won't see us."

31
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.371
Cole nodded.

32
00:01:50.391 --> 00:01:51.992
"Don't forget the flour."

33
00:01:53.633 --> 00:01:56.236
Henry picked up the bag of flour sitting by his feet.

34
00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.582
Nathan had borrowed it from his family's kitchen.

35
00:02:01.063 --> 00:02:03.044
It was an important part of Henry's plan.

36
00:02:03.064 --> 00:02:05.706
"I've got it," Henry said.

37
00:02:05.726 --> 00:02:07.167
"Let's go."

38
00:02:13.691 --> 00:02:17.614
That evening Henry and Maggie met Cole at Nora's house again.

39
00:02:18.594 --> 00:02:19.875
They all hid behind the hedge.

40
00:02:21.376 --> 00:02:23.778
It was time for step two of Henry's plan.

41
00:02:23.798 --> 00:02:25.779
"Is Nathan coming?"

42
00:02:26.019 --> 00:02:26.780
Cole whispered.

43
00:02:27.852 --> 00:02:28.773
Henry shook his head.

44
00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:32.075
"I told him to stay inside and act normal.

45
00:02:33.096 --> 00:02:35.197
That might keep Nora from getting suspicious."

46
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:38.259
"Good idea," Maggie said.

47
00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:43.503
"If he's home when she goes to bed, she'll never think we're still investigating her."

48
00:02:45.044 --> 00:02:45.745
Henry nodded.

49
00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.866
"Let's get to the tree house."

50
00:02:50.588 --> 00:02:53.190
Soon all three of them were in Nathan's tree house.

51
00:02:54.611 --> 00:02:55.872
Cole went over to the window.

52
00:02:56.972 --> 00:02:59.113
"All we have to do now is wait," he said.

53
00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:04.255
"We can take turns watching for Nora to come outside," Henry suggested.

54
00:03:04.275 --> 00:03:07.156
"I'll go first," Cole said.

55
00:03:07.176 --> 00:03:11.018
"You two probably won't even have to take turns.

56
00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.839
Last time Nora sneaked out right after she went to bed."

57
00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.641
Maggie nodded, looking hopeful.

58
00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:22.683
"Maybe I'll get home in time to see my TV show after all," she said.

59
00:03:22.703 --> 00:03:26.884
"It's not on until eight-thirty."

60
00:03:26.904 --> 00:03:29.006
"I thought you were recording it," Cole said.

61
00:03:29.026 --> 00:03:31.928
"I am," Maggie replied.

62
00:03:31.948 --> 00:03:34.369
"But I'd rather see it live."

63
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.751
They all settled down to wait.

64
00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:43.135
Cole sat by the window watching the house while Henry and Maggie played cards.

65
00:03:44.376 --> 00:03:45.437
Half an hour passed.

66
00:03:46.697 --> 00:03:47.578
Cole stretched.

67
00:03:47.598 --> 00:03:50.980
"I'm bored," he said.

68
00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.622
"It's time for somebody else to take a turn."

69
00:03:53.642 --> 00:03:56.204
"I'll do it," Henry offered.

70
00:03:57.228 --> 00:03:58.689
He traded places with Cole.

71
00:04:00.151 --> 00:04:02.212
When he looked out, the yard was quiet.

72
00:04:03.794 --> 00:04:08.958
From the tree house, it was easy to see the back door, the playroom window, and Nora's bedroom

73
00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:12.041
window. Another half hour went by.

74
00:04:13.262 --> 00:04:15.824
Henry's eyes were getting tired from staring at the house.

75
00:04:15.844 --> 00:04:20.608
"Maybe Nora isn't going to sneak out tonight," he said.

76
00:04:22.149 --> 00:04:25.092
Cole looked up from flipping through one of Nathan's comic books.

77
00:04:26.448 --> 00:04:28.969
"Or maybe she was telling us the truth," he said.

78
00:04:28.989 --> 00:04:33.051
"Maybe she really was sneaking out to drink soda in that shed."

79
00:04:34.212 --> 00:04:37.173
Henry still didn't believe Nora's story about the soda.

80
00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:39.394
It didn't seem logical.

81
00:04:40.414 --> 00:04:42.515
But Nora wasn't a very logical person.

82
00:04:43.596 --> 00:04:44.556
Could Cole be right?

83
00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:49.158
"It's probably after eight o'clock by now," said Maggie.

84
00:04:49.178 --> 00:04:53.100
"I'll have to leave soon if I want to watch my show."

85
00:04:54.416 --> 00:04:57.257
"Let's just wait another few minutes," Henry said.

86
00:04:57.277 --> 00:05:00.538
"Maybe Nora is being extra careful.

87
00:05:01.598 --> 00:05:03.919
Her parents are probably checking on her a lot."

88
00:05:05.099 --> 00:05:05.999
He looked out again.

89
00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.140
It was getting darker, and there were deep shadows in the woods.

90
00:05:11.221 --> 00:05:13.341
But it was still easy to see Nora's house.

91
00:05:14.682 --> 00:05:16.102
Finally Maggie stood up.

92
00:05:17.222 --> 00:05:18.042
"I'm going home.

93
00:05:19.623 --> 00:05:23.264
There's no point in missing my show if Nora's not going to sneak out tonight."

94
00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.565
Henry was disappointed.

95
00:05:26.665 --> 00:05:30.867
He and Cole had spent a long time setting up their special detective trick.

96
00:05:31.947 --> 00:05:33.728
They'd used the whole bag of flour!

97
00:05:33.748 --> 00:05:39.691
"Maybe you're right and she's not going to sneak out tonight," he said with a sigh.

98
00:05:40.811 --> 00:05:42.672
He glanced at the house one more time.

99
00:05:43.692 --> 00:05:44.533
Then he gasped.

100
00:05:45.633 --> 00:05:46.954
"Wait!" he whispered.

101
00:05:46.974 --> 00:05:48.975
"Here she comes!"

102
00:05:48.995 --> 00:05:51.676
"Really?" Maggie said.

103
00:05:52.804 --> 00:05:54.545
She and Cole rushed to the window.

104
00:05:56.026 --> 00:06:00.369
They all watched Nora climb out her bedroom window and hurry across the backyard.

105
00:06:00.389 --> 00:06:04.431
"She's heading straight for the woods," Maggie whispered.

106
00:06:05.472 --> 00:06:06.212
Cole nodded.

107
00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:09.494
"She's definitely not heading toward the soda shed!"

108
00:06:10.495 --> 00:06:11.415
Henry smiled.

109
00:06:12.376 --> 00:06:13.637
His feeling had been right!

110
00:06:15.638 --> 00:06:18.980
Now all they had to do was figure out what Nora was really doing.
